          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PRO 27:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Look after your sheep and cattle as carefully as you can, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PRO.27.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PRO.27.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PRO 27:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "because wealth is not permanent. Not even nations last for ever. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PRO.27.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PRO.27.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PRO 27:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You cut the hay and then cut the grass on the hillsides while the next crop of hay is growing. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PRO.27.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PRO.27.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PRO 27:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You can make clothes from the wool of your sheep and buy land with the money you get from selling some of your goats. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PRO.27.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PRO.27.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PRO 27:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The rest of the goats will provide milk for you and your family, and for your servant women as well.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PRO.27.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PRO.27.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
